{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/935995-the-great-flock-talons-of-horus","id":935995,"title":"The Great Flock (Talons of Horus)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-23T02:07:27-07:00","id":935995,"title":"The Great Flock (Talons of Horus)","content":"Hey guys, I play in a crossover between WtA/MtA, my character is a kinfolk Dreamspeaker (with Spirit 5, meaning he can get past the Horizon into the Deep Umbra and allow others to do so); a reference to this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Habitat: The Talons have an affinity with the Deep Umbra and grow in number, the deeper it gets. The Great Flock itself disappeared beyond the Horizon and has not been seen since 1349, at the height of the Black Plague in Europe. Some theorize that the Great Flock ranges the Deep Umbra, protecting Gaia from creatures beyond the Horizon. A few claim the Great Flock will only return at the Apocalypse. </div> </div> </div>As the chronicle nears to Reckoning/Apocalypse plot, he intended to gain Falcon's grace and if successful lead the Great Flock of the Talons of Horus back into Earth to have them fight strategically against the bigger threats. My question is, Axis Mundi offers the following stats:<br /> <br /> <b>Large Flock:</b> Rage 8, Gnosis 10, Willpower 8, Power 95;<br /> <br /> ...but for when it's to do with the the Great Flock it only says &quot;unknown&quot;. Wanted to ask if any of you ever storytold the Great Flock, what stats did you use, and if not, what you think should be reasonable keeping in mind few characters are already high-powered (the setting has been going on for years, Elders with a few rank 5 gifts, two archmages with Arete 6 and such).<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12152-rotwood","user":"Rotwood","date":". 07-23-2016, 05:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12152-rotwood","name":"Rotwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T23:14:31-07:00","id":936434,"title":"","content":"It's a storyteller plot device. It does whatever you want them to do. Once the PC is able to bring the Great Flock to the Realm, you should use them however you want to use them to alter the game setting or create plot. If you are not ready to deal with that yet, then the PC can't do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}